WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.560
CAESAR

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.960
Caesar Clown is often named as one of the
prime candidates as a possible next straw

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.460
hat. And while I believe that he in theory
fulfils the basic requirements for this, I

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:22.699
think his character serves a completely different
purpose in the story after all.

00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:32.579
There aren’t all too many parallels to draw
between the lord of the rings and One Piece,

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:39.140
two of my all-time favourite works of fiction.
One thing however, that both of these worlds

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.050
undoudabtlay share is their seeming disregard
and even distaste for science and scientific

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:51.320
advancement in their epic world building.
While there clearly is some scientific progress

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:57.400
in both worlds, it tends to be associated
with military power, destruction and an overall

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:03.790
threat to the vast beauty and pureness of
a world, where strength, courage and WILL

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:08.799
determine one’s success in battle, and where
the heroes strive to forge a path to peace

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:13.520
and freedom. After all, we don’t want to
see a world where Aragon drives around in

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:19.630
a corvette, ordering drone strikes on Mordor.
In the lord of the rings, the best example

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:25.740
for stark technological and industrial progress
is Saruman, who’s ambitious undertakings

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:32.560
to wage war, go hand in hand with the destruction
of the environment, that in the end fights

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:45.381
back against him. And bringing this all the
way back to One Piece, the face of Science

00:01:45.381 --> 00:01:55.700
and technical advancement in One Piece is
of course none other than - Dr. Vegapunk.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:03.590
Yes, it’s without any doubt the biggest
tragedy of Caesar’s character that even

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:09.160
as the archetypical mad scientist-type of
antagonist, he is not the dominant face of

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:14.560
Science in One Piece. His arc is arguably
the most insignificant after the time skip

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:21.530
and his battle with the straw hats was not
exactly a close call. And yet Caesar has stuck

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:28.239
around for 4 consecutive arcs in the story,
going from Punk hazard, over Dressrosa and

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:34.189
Zou all the Way to Whole cake Island, traveling
together with the crew and developing his

00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:39.840
own dynamic with Luffy and co until he finally
was free to go his own way after the events

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:47.239
of the Wedding. It is no wonder then, that
similar to characters like Momo or Vivi, Caesar

00:02:47.239 --> 00:02:53.349
for the longest time was a top contender for
the next spot on the Sunny. And while I strongly

00:02:53.349 --> 00:02:58.370
believe that Caesar wouldn’t be a great
fit for the crew, as we’ll see over the

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:04.040
course of this video, I also think that people
who straight-out disregarded this as a realistic

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:11.230
option, have overlooked some crucial aspects
of his character. Because Caesar in fact fulfils

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:17.480
a number of general qualifications strongly
associated with becoming a straw hat: Having

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:24.130
a quirk, a dream and a tragic backstory. If
you’re shaking your head at this, let me

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:30.340
convince you otherwise. Oh yeah and before
we get into it, if you haven’t subscribed

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:42.079
to the channel yet, make sure to hit that
big red button below this video.

00:03:42.079 --> 00:03:47.420
I think we don’t have to say too much about
Caesar being the sort of quirky addition to

00:03:47.420 --> 00:04:00.969
the crew that Luffy loves to make. His strange
appearance, his logia devil fruit as well

00:04:00.969 --> 00:04:06.840
as his socially awkward personality undoubtedly
would make him a great fit among a talking

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:12.959
Skeleton, a pervy Cyborg and a candy-loving
reindeer. So we can definitely cross this

00:04:12.959 --> 00:04:24.050
one off the list. What about the tragic backstory
then?

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:28.830
Here it might already be less obvious for
some people. However, as we will explore in

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:36.520
more detail later on, Caesar does indeed have
a tragic backstory. It’s undeniable that

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:42.389
he is actually a quite intelligent and academically
capable person that has dedicated his entire

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:50.250
life to science and research. And yet despite
all that he is outshone by Vegapunk for what

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:56.400
is basically his entire professional life.
There seems to be nothing that he can surpass

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.810
him in and he suffers heavily under the disregard
people have for him, always in the shadow

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:08.039
of this OTHE brilliant scientist that is creating
technology 500 years ahead of the current

00:05:08.039 --> 00:05:14.410
age. Given his psychopathic and apathetic
personality, that is yearning for attention

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:20.789
and recognition, I think we can pretty safely
assume that Caesar didn’t exactly have the

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:27.080
most fun childhood as well. This is also where
the theme of Julius Caesar come into play,

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:32.979
who served as a namesake for the character
and might hint at some sort of betrayal happening

00:05:32.979 --> 00:05:40.039
in his past. And so, while it might not compare
to the likes of Robin or Brook, I think Caesar’s

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:47.550
life and past can definitely be crossed off
as tragic. So, what about the infamous dream,

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:54.289
that every straw hat needs. Surely Ohara isn’t
proposing that Caesar has a dream - and also

00:05:54.289 --> 00:06:05.629
why is Ohara referring to himself in the third
person?

00:06:05.629 --> 00:06:12.330
Now, this speech here that Caesar holds in
front of his men whose demise and suffering

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:19.889
HE caused HIMSELF, is OBVIOUSLY meant to be
pretence. We know that Caesar in fact doesn’t

00:06:19.889 --> 00:06:25.139
care about his men one bit and that HE was
the one who launched the horrendous explosion

00:06:25.139 --> 00:06:30.669
on the island and not Vegapunk. However, I
think that there are parts in this speech

00:06:30.669 --> 00:06:35.830
that might very well be honest, regardless
of whether Caesar is aware of that himself

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:44.240
or not. He clearly DOES want to surpass Vegapunk
and wishes for more attention. And so I personally

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:49.220
believe that the part where he talks about
his dream to bring peace to the world trough

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:56.819
science is also true, or at least WAS true
at some point in time. I think it’s not

00:06:56.819 --> 00:07:01.940
too far fetched that Caesar’s passion for
Science didn’t start with a minority complex

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:08.360
towards Vegapunk right away, but with the
amazement and joy of experimenting, - a young

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:14.750
boy with the hopes to make the world a better
place and loosing his path along the way.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:28.120
I think there is a quite strong argument for
this dream to be the truth. So, clearly the

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:33.389
argument that Caesar might become a member
of the crew is not completely empty. With

00:07:33.389 --> 00:07:40.639
a quirky and interesting character, a tragic
past and an unfulfilled and seemingly unachievable

00:07:40.639 --> 00:07:46.930
dream, Caesar certainly could fit into the
ranks of the straw hats. So, what then makes

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:58.280
me SO certain, that he won’t ever join the
crew?

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:04.530
Caesar in many ways is a quite straightforward
character, fulfilling the trope of the mad

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:10.260
scientist that doesn’t shy aways from unethical
methods to satisfy his urge for discovery.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:15.729
In close connection with his Gas devil fruit
powers, he is a quite toxic and at the same

00:08:15.729 --> 00:08:22.610
time elusive character. In many ways he is
literally all hot air, relying on trickery

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:30.169
and more powerful people for protection. Nonetheless,
his genius is real, and despite his hedonistic

00:08:30.169 --> 00:08:36.620
lifestyle, he is the ONLY one able to produce
the chemical SAD for Doflamingo’s artificial

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:44.940
devil fruits and thus is a priceless asset
for both Dofi and Kaido. For this, Doflamingo

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:50.829
even threatened Monet with death, if she let
anything happen to Caesar and made it a priority

00:08:50.829 --> 00:09:04.130
to retrieve Caesar upon his defeat. The TURE
reason why Caesar can never be a straw hat

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:09.910
however, lies in the rarely mentioned, but
in my opinion most important qualification

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:17.470
for any straw hat: Being changed by Luffy.
All of the current straw hats, without one.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:22.649
single. exception. have been influenced by
Luffy and have had a significant change of

00:09:22.649 --> 00:09:29.330
heart or turnaround in their life upon meeting
him. Luffy literally changed all their lives

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:34.930
to the better. In other words, all members
of the crew have a positive character arc,

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:42.070
that ends on a high note when officially joining
the crew. And Caesar simply doesn’t have

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:57.470
that. Despite traveling with Luffy for so
long, his character arc is undeniably flat.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:03.529
As any well-written character he does have
a Lie about the world that he believes in,

00:10:03.529 --> 00:10:09.550
that he is a better Scientist than Vegapunk,
unfairly looked down upon and thus compelled

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:16.510
to beat him at everything he does. Clearly
this is not true. As is shown over and over

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:23.019
again, Vegapunk seems to be the better scientist.
Momo’s artificial devil fruit was way better

00:10:23.019 --> 00:10:30.930
than any of the smiles. The numbers are way
better than any of Caesar’s attempt of gigantification.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:35.940
And there was a reason that he wanted to get
his hands on Franky and the laser Vegapunk

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:41.410
had developed. Yet, despite being confronted
with this truth through his encounters with

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:49.079
Luffy, he never stops to consider that he
might use his intelligence in other ways to

00:10:49.079 --> 00:10:55.790
follow his dream. That he’s actually holding
himself back with his obsession with vegapunk.

00:10:55.790 --> 00:11:01.389
Oda put him in the exact same spot as the
other straw hat’s, giving him the chance

00:11:01.389 --> 00:11:16.360
to develop, but he never does. This is of
course not bad writing, but a conscious decision

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:23.350
of character design. But in my eyes, and I
would say also in Oda’s, it disqualifies

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:34.630
him as a future straw hat. So if Caesar’s
purpose is not to join the crew? What is?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:43.640
Caesar’s character serves a number of important
purposes in the story. He goes from a light

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:50.579
version of Hisoka, who’s video will be coming
soon, to Buggy over the course of Punk hazard,

00:11:50.579 --> 00:11:55.459
adding a comedic element to the straw hats’
more and more serious journey into the new

00:11:55.459 --> 00:12:08.660
world. Oda sacrifices a lot of his character’s
potential during Punk Hazard for setting up

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:14.590
the bigger fish during the Yonko saga. As
a result, Caesar is introduced as a supplier

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:21.620
for Doflamingo, Big Mom and Kaido alike, pointing
towards the increasingly intense arcs that

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:28.350
will follow Punk Hazard. Doflamingo in particular
steals his show by arriving on the island

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:41.131
in person, threatening to take over the entire
arc if not for Aokiji’s interference. As

00:12:41.131 --> 00:12:47.480
a result Caesar’s role in the story is reduced
to a setup-villain that serves as a measuring

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:54.190
stick for the true threats yet to come. Is
his character useless then? Did Oda ruin the

00:12:54.190 --> 00:13:01.699
potential he had? Honestly, I would say a
bit, yes. Caesar could have been a way more

00:13:01.699 --> 00:13:08.209
interesting villain, especially if Punk Hazard
had been a little bit more condensed. However,

00:13:08.209 --> 00:13:13.860
I think the real message behind his character
is something completely different, that often

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:26.240
gets lost under all these other layers.
Drawing the line all the way back to the beginning

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:32.470
of the video, I believe that Caesar, despite
his inferiority to Vegapunk, is supposed to

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:38.649
represent the face of science and technological
advancement in One Piece. In a world where

00:13:38.649 --> 00:13:44.839
pirates sail on boatsfrom island to island,
fighting with swords and shooting cannons,

00:13:44.839 --> 00:13:51.420
there suddenly is laser technology and biochemical
weapons of mass destruction. Something that

00:13:51.420 --> 00:14:02.329
seemingly doesn’t fit into the world building
and disturbs the adventure-like world we are

00:14:02.329 --> 00:14:09.839
exploring. While Oda repeatedly hints that
before the void century, science might have

00:14:09.839 --> 00:14:16.279
been way more advanced and possibly used for
the good, at this point in time it is mainly

00:14:16.279 --> 00:14:22.210
used for military purposes, bringing an unfair
advantage into battles that are otherwise

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:36.140
decided through willpower, strength and the
use of mythical devil fruits. Caesar, as one

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:41.540
of the leading scientific forces, sets off
a chemical weapon on Punk Hazard, killing

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:47.779
or crippling most of its inhabitants and destroying
its environment,&nbsp;selling or creating weapons

00:14:47.779 --> 00:14:53.490
of mass destruction for similarly unscrupulous
individuals such as&nbsp;Doflamingo, performs

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:58.389
sick experiments on children and drugs them
with&nbsp;a lethal, addictive drug&nbsp;to ensure

00:14:58.389 --> 00:15:04.290
that they do not run away, and ultimately
tries to murder everyone on Punk Hazard so

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:11.140
he could test out his new&nbsp;weapon-pet,&nbsp;Smiley—all
of which he does without a shred of remorse

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:18.480
or empathy for his potential victims. And
leading into the current Wano Arc, he is responsible

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:24.040
for the creation of the mutative artificial
SMILE devil fruits that either turn their

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:32.050
users into grotesque hybrid creatures or condemns
them to a live unable to show any other emotion

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:47.449
than laughter. Oda paints a very dark picture
of science through Caesar’s character, emphasising

00:15:47.449 --> 00:15:53.330
the adventure and freedom aspect of a more
simple and untouched world, filled with exotic

00:15:53.330 --> 00:16:06.070
places that have to be explored by ship.
And in addition to that Caesar also leaves

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:12.370
us with two very interesting options for Vegapunk,
who dismissed him as his assistant due to

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:18.530
his unethical behaviour, that is one of the
most heatedly discussed issues to this day.

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:25.529
Is Vegapunk good or bad. Given the hints we
have gotten from Oda so far it seems that

00:16:25.529 --> 00:16:33.339
Vegapunk is secretly helping the revolutionaries
and passively aiding the straw hats. However,

00:16:33.339 --> 00:16:39.589
I think there is a quite notable chance that
Vegapunk might be the true evil genius of

00:16:39.589 --> 00:16:44.399
the story, that is actually way more ruthless
and unethical than Caesar, as he is the one

00:16:44.399 --> 00:16:49.670
responsible for all those horrendous experimentations
in the first place, that Caesar is trying

00:16:49.670 --> 00:17:02.040
to imitate - not even mentioning the work
he conducted together with Judge Vinsmoke.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:06.720
And so, even though he is often not out at
first place by people, when it comes to science

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:13.320
&amp; industrial process in the story, he undoubtedly
introduces us to countless important concepts

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:18.510
and insights about the role that technology
plays in the story. In conclusion I think

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:22.820
that Caesar is a quite unique and important
character in the story, that hasn’t been

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:28.910
used to its full potential. Oda teased his
readers with the quite real possibility of

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:34.910
becoming the next straw hat, but in the end
made it clear that you can’t join the crew

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:38.400
without correcting the path you walk first.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:43.830
Ironically enough, Luffy is able to open the
eyes of caesar’s protector in the next arc

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:55.951
that follows. If you want to learn the true
meaning of the bird cage for Doflamingo, make

00:17:55.951 --> 00:18:00.500
sure to check out his video here. Thanks guys.
Peace.

